@title Dead or Alive Xtreme 3 Venus - Day 1, beach volleyball
@game  PCSH00250
@shot-every 100   # shots through the run so a human can assess render quality
@watch location u32 0x8178c788   # the activity-menu location card: 0 Niki Beach, 1 Tranquil Beach, 2 Pool, 4 Sports Shop

# ============================================================================
# WHAT THIS RECIPE DOES
# Boots through the logos and the intro (autosave dialog, title screen, the island
# arrival scenes and the Day 1 tutorial pages), steps the activity menu to NIKI BEACH,
# picks PLAY BEACH VOLLEYBALL, starts the game from its controls screen and plays a
# match by alternating circle (receive / toss) and cross (spike / serve).
#
# HOW IT WAS AUTHORED
# - Boot: a circle TAP every 150 frames from 800 to 4750. A held press is ONE press to
#   this title, so every press has a release line. The taps answer the autosave dialog
#   (circle = confirm on the Asia build), PRESS ANY BUTTON, the menu's first entry
#   (Travel to New Zack Island) and every dialogue / tutorial page up to "Activity 2".
# - The activity menu opens on a location the title PICKS AT RANDOM: under SMP the pick
#   follows thread timing, so runs land on Pool, Niki Beach or Tranquil Beach. RIGHT steps
#   the location card (Pool -> Niki Beach -> Tranquil Beach -> Sports Shop). The
#   `location` watch was found by value search over four dumps of one one-baton run, one
#   per RIGHT press (VITASLOP_MEM_DUMP_AT with several frames): a u32 in the image's own
#   data, so its address does not move. `@wait watch location == 0 pulse right 40` holds
#   the input until the card reads Niki Beach.
# - Niki Beach's list is Relax / Play Beach Volleyball / Play Beach Flags: circle opens
#   it, DOWN + circle picks volleyball. Its controls screen says cross = START GAME,
#   circle = receive / toss, square = receive and attack, cross = spike / block / serve.
# ============================================================================

